{"reference":"Psalms 130","book":"Psalms","chapter":130,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"The Songs of Ascents","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Psalm 130 belongs among the Songs of Ascents in Psalms 120–134. These surrounding psalms include communal memories of sanctuary destruction and Babylonian exile, alongside thanksgiving for return, festival praise, meditation on Torah, and songs oriented toward worship. This wider setting is disputed, but it situates Psalm 130’s plea and hope within a collection that also gives voice to communal worship and restoration.","verse_refs":["Psalms 120:1-7","Psalms 121:1-8","Psalms 122:1-9","Psalms 123:1-4","Psalms 124:1-8","Psalms 125:1-5","Psalms 126:1-6","Psalms 127:1-5","Psalms 128:1-6","Psalms 129:1-8","Psalms 131:1-3","Psalms 132:1-18","Psalms 133:1-3","Psalms 134:1-3"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_psalms_130_da23136acc2ddd1b9b419d84"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}